{#-
  CowSwap Milkman — submit price-protected swap orders.

  Uses the Chainlink DynamicSlippageChecker (aliases.curator.price_checker) as the
  pinned price checker. Its priceCheckerData is ABI-encoded as
  (uint256 slippageBps, bytes innerData), where innerData is itself
  abi.encode(address[] feeds, bool[] reverses) — the price oracle the slippage
  check measures the swap against. The policy bounds slippageBps per destination
  token AND pins innerData to the exact feed configuration for the pair.

  Pinning innerData is load-bearing, not cosmetic: the slippage cap is a bound
  relative to whatever price the feeds report. If innerData were left free, a
  compromised role member could supply a feed reporting a fair price of ~0, so
  "lose no more than slippageBps" would permit swapping the Safe's tokens for
  ~nothing and still clear the gate. Nothing downstream (Milkman, the checker,
  its calculator) restricts the feed addresses, so the policy must.

  Required params:
    from_tokens — list of TOKEN alias keys the Safe may approve to Milkman and
                  swap from (e.g. ["USDC"]).
    to_tokens   — list of destination tokens, each with its own slippage cap and
                  the exact Chainlink feed path used to price the swap:
                    - token: <TOKEN key>
                      max_slippage_bps: <int>      # e.g. 500 ≡ ≤ 5%
                      feeds: [<feed addr>, ...]    # the price path, in order
                      reverses: [<bool>, ...]      # one per feed; same length
                  feeds/reverses must equal exactly what the swap submits for this
                  pair (see RequestMilkmanSwap): e.g. USDC → PYUSD uses
                  feeds: [USDC/USD, PYUSD/USD], reverses: [false, true].

  Swap allow-list: the cartesian product from_tokens × to_tokens (via the
  `milkman_pairs` filter), with self-pairs (from == to.token) removed so that
  listing a token in BOTH lists (buy + sell) never emits a nonsensical X → X
  branch. One `matches` per (from, to); wrapped in an `or` when there are ≥ 2,
  or emitted as a plain `matches` when exactly 1 (a 1-branch `or` is degenerate
  and rejected at apply time). Each branch binds the cap and feeds to its pair.

  Optional params:
    max_approval — exclusive upper bound (in base units) for the approve `amount`
                   on every from-token, emitted as `less_than max_approval`.
                   Defaults to uint256.max, which only rules out the literal
                   infinite-approval sentinel and does NOT bound exposure. Set it to
                   a realistic operational ceiling to cap how much the role can
                   approve to Milkman in one shot. A single value applies to all
                   from_tokens, so it is most precise with one from-token (the
                   common case); with mixed decimals, pick a bound valid for each.

  Policy enforced:
    approve(spender=Milkman, amount < max_approval) on each from-token.
    requestSwapExactTokensForTokens, per (from, to) branch:
      amountIn     pass
      fromToken    == aliases.tokens[from]
      toToken      == aliases.tokens[to.token]
      to           == avatar (proceeds stay in the Safe)
      appData      pass (CoW Protocol order metadata, set at runtime)
      priceChecker == aliases.curator.price_checker (Chainlink DynamicSlippageChecker)
      priceCheckerData → abi_encoded:
        slippageBps  < to.max_slippage_bps + 1   (i.e. ≤ to.max_slippage_bps)
        innerData    == abi.encode(to.feeds, to.reverses)

    Note: cancelSwap is NOT included. Milkman's cancelSwap targets the per-swap
    order clone (address unknown at policy-creation time), so it cannot be
    pre-authorised; cancellations are executed directly through the Safe UI.
-#}
{%- macro swap_params(from, to) -%}
- name: amountIn
  operator: "pass"
- name: fromToken
  operator: "equal_to"
  value: "{{ aliases.tokens[from] }}"
  value_type: "address"
- name: toToken
  operator: "equal_to"
  value: "{{ aliases.tokens[to.token] }}"
  value_type: "address"
- name: to
  operator: "equal_to_avatar"
- name: appData
  operator: "pass"
- name: priceChecker
  operator: "equal_to"
  value: "{{ aliases.curator.price_checker }}"
  value_type: "address"
- name: priceCheckerData
  param_type: "abi_encoded"
  children:
    - name: slippageBps
      param_type: "static"
      operator: "less_than"
      value: "{{ to.max_slippage_bps + 1 }}"
      value_type: "uint256"
    - name: innerData
      param_type: "dynamic"
      operator: "equal_to"
      value: "{{ [to.feeds, to.reverses] | abi_encode(['address[]', 'bool[]']) }}"
      value_type: "bytes"
      # display-only: lets `zac plan` decode the pinned blob back to (feeds, reverses).
      display_decode:
        - { name: feeds, type: "address[]" }
        - { name: reverses, type: "bool[]" }
{%- endmacro -%}
roles:
{%- for token in from_tokens %}
  - address: "{{ aliases.tokens[token] }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function approve(address spender, uint256 amount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: spender
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ aliases.curator.milkman }}"
            value_type: "address"
          - name: amount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "less_than"
            value: "{{ max_approval | default('115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639935') }}"
            value_type: "uint256"
{%- endfor %}

  - address: "{{ aliases.curator.milkman }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function requestSwapExactTokensForTokens(uint256 amountIn, address fromToken, address toToken, address to, bytes32 appData, address priceChecker, bytes priceCheckerData)"
        execution_options: "none"
{%- set pairs = from_tokens | milkman_pairs(to_tokens) %}
{%- if pairs | length == 1 %}
        operator: "matches"
        params:
{{ swap_params(pairs[0].from, pairs[0].to) | indent(10, true) }}
{%- else %}
        operator: "or"
        branches:
{%- for pair in pairs %}
          - operator: "matches"
            params:
{{ swap_params(pair.from, pair.to) | indent(14, true) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
